.view-switch{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:14px 18px;margin-top:15px}.view-switch-label{color:#5b6770;font-size:13px;font-weight:650}.view-switch a{display:inline-block;padding:6px 11px;border-radius:6px;background:#1769aa;color:#fff;text-decoration:none}.view-switch a:hover{background:#12334d}.interactive-hint{color:#5b6770;font-size:13px;margin:5px 0 12px}.company-filter-controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:7px 0 2px}.company-filter-controls label{font-weight:650;color:#12334d}.company-filter-controls select{font:inherit;padding:5px 9px;border:1px solid #b8c7cf;border-radius:6px;background:#fff}.mover-panel{border:1px solid #cfe1e4;background:#f4fbfb;border-radius:9px;padding:12px 15px;min-height:42px}.mover-panel h4{margin:0 0 7px;font-size:15px;color:#12334d}.mover-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:6px 18px;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none}.mover-list li{font-size:13px}.mover-list .change{color:#168f8a;font-weight:700}.main-rate-point{cursor:pointer;outline:none}.main-rate-point:focus,.main-rate-point:hover{stroke:#d97706;stroke-width:3;r:7}.sector-toggle{border:1px solid transparent;background:transparent;color:#5b6770;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font:inherit;font-size:13px}.sector-toggle:hover,.sector-toggle.is-active{background:#e8f5f4;border-color:#b9d9d7;color:#12334d}.sector-toggle.is-muted{opacity:.4}.sector-line{transition:opacity .18s ease,stroke-width .18s ease}.sector-line.is-muted{opacity:.12}.sector-line.is-active{stroke-width:4.5}.sector-reset{margin:8px 0 0;padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid #b8c7cf;background:#fff;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;color:#1769aa}.hist-controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:4px 0 12px}.hist-controls label{font-weight:650;color:#12334d}.hist-controls select{font:inherit;padding:5px 9px;border:1px solid #b8c7cf;border-radius:6px;background:#fff}.hist-summary{color:#5b6770;font-size:13px;margin-top:5px}.hist-bar{fill:#168f8a;fill-opacity:.82}.hist-bar:hover{fill:#1769aa}.hist-curve{fill:none;stroke:#d97706;stroke-width:3;stroke-dasharray:7 5}.hist-sigma-line{stroke:#8b98a3;stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:4 4}.hist-mean-line{stroke:#c2416b;stroke-width:2}.hist-outliers{border-top:1px solid #dce3e8;margin-top:14px;padding-top:10px}.hist-outliers h4{margin:0 0 5px;font-size:15px;color:#12334d}.hist-outliers ul{margin:5px 0 0;padding-left:20px}.hist-outlier-toggle{padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid #b8c7cf;background:#fff;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;color:#1769aa}.scatter-point{cursor:pointer;transition:r .12s ease,fill-opacity .12s ease}.scatter-point:hover{r:7;fill-opacity:1}.axis-label{font-size:12px;fill:#5b6770}
</style></head><body><main>
<header><h1>Regulatory burden in a balanced $PanelName panel</h1><p class='dek'>Thematic coding, frame analysis and keyword content analysis of annual reports from 2015 through 2025. To make the time series comparable, the report includes only companies with a complete report for every year in the 11-year window.</p><div class='meta'><span class='pill'>$($total.Reports) reports</span><span class='pill'>$($complete.Count) companies</span><span class='pill'>2015-2025</span><span class='pill'>Generated $(Get-Date -Format 'd MMMM yyyy')</span></div></header>
<div class='callout'><strong>Executive reading.</strong> This balanced-panel design separates changes in disclosure language from changes in sample composition. The measures are textual salience - not observed regulatory expenditure. The selected companies discuss regulation mainly as an obligation translated into controls, reporting, systems and assurance; explicit references to "burden" are much rarer than references to requirements, regulators and compliance infrastructure.</div>
$viewSwitchHtml
<h2>1. Scope and coding method</h2><div class='panel'><p>The corpus is <code>$archiveDisplay</code>. At generation time, <strong>$($complete.Count) companies</strong> had valid PDF files for all 11 years from 2015 to 2025, producing <strong>$($total.Reports) reports</strong>. Companies with even one missing year were excluded from every table and chart, rather than contributing only their available reports.</p><p>PDF text was extracted with Poppler <code>pdftotext</code>, normalized for whitespace and split into sentence-like passages. A passage entered the regulatory-burden set when it contained a direct regulatory/compliance cue or when reporting, audit, control, process or systems language co-occurred with an obligation, requirement, cost or rule cue. Passages can receive multiple thematic codes.</p><ul><li><strong>Content analysis:</strong> counts six tracked lexical families - regulation, compliance, burden, requirement, regulator and legislation - and reports rates per 100,000 extracted words.</li><li><strong>Thematic coding:</strong> ten themes identify the organisational work through which rules are interpreted and implemented.</li><li><strong>Frame analysis:</strong> each selected passage receives one primary rhetorical frame: cost/challenge, obligation/control, transition/anticipation, opportunity/legitimacy, or descriptive/neutral.</li></ul><p class='note'>This is a transparent rule-based first pass. Different report lengths, sector vocabulary, repeated risk disclosures and PDF extraction quality affect counts. A missing term is not evidence that a company has no regulatory burden.</p></div>
<h2>2. Corpus and year-by-year content analysis</h2><div class='grid'><div class='metric'><div class='n'>$($total.Reports)</div><div class='l'>annual reports coded</div></div><div class='metric'><div class='n'>$($complete.Count)</div><div class='l'>companies in balanced panel</div></div><div class='metric'><div class='n'>$(Num $total.Words)</div><div class='l'>extracted words</div></div><div class='metric'><div class='n'>$(Num $total.Coded)</div><div class='l'>coded regulatory passages</div></div></div>
<div class='panel'><h3>Regulatory incidence per 100,000 words</h3><div class='chart'><svg id='annual-incidence-chart' viewBox='0 0 1000 340' role='img' aria-label='Six tracked regulatory term occurrences per 100,000 extracted words from 2015 through 2025'>$( $grid.ToString() )<polyline id='annual-incidence-line' points='$($pts -join ' ')' fill='none' stroke='#1769aa' stroke-width='4' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-linecap='round'/>$( $dots.ToString() )$( $labels.ToString() )<text x='515' y='326' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' fill='#5b6770'>Six tracked terms per 100,000 extracted words; y-axis $(One $yMin)-$(One $yMax)</text></svg></div><p class='interactive-hint'>Hover over, or keyboard-focus, a year point to see the five companies with the largest year-over-year increase in six-term salience, including their percentage growth.</p><div id='mover-panel' class='mover-panel' aria-live='polite'></div><p class='caption'>The line normalizes the combined appearances of regulation, compliance, burden, requirement, regulator and legislation by report length. Each point represents the same balanced group of $($complete.Count) companies, so rises and falls are less likely to be artefacts of companies entering or leaving the dataset. The rate peaks in <strong>$($peakYear.Name)</strong> at <strong>$(One $peakYear.Value)</strong> terms per 100,000 words.</p></div>
<div class='panel'><h3>Which regulatory words drive the index?</h3><div class='chart'><svg viewBox='0 0 1000 320' role='img' aria-label='Separate lines for regulation, compliance, burden, requirement, regulator and legislation rates per 100,000 words from 2015 through 2025'>$( $termGrid.ToString() )$( $termSeries.ToString() )$( $labels.ToString() )<text x='515' y='312' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' fill='#5b6770'>Individual term-family rates per 100,000 extracted words; y-axis 0-$(One $termYMax)</text></svg></div><div class='legend'>$($termLegend.ToString())</div><p class='caption'>The combined index can conceal substitution between terms. This panel separates the trajectories: a rise in <em>regulation</em> may reflect direct discussion of rules, while <em>compliance</em> and <em>requirement</em> more often capture the organisation's response. <em>Burden</em> is deliberately retained as its own line because it is an explicit evaluative term and is expected to be much less frequent than procedural language.</p></div>
<div class='panel'><h3>Year-by-year totals</h3><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Year</th><th class='num'>Reports</th><th class='num'>Words</th><th class='num'>Regulation</th><th class='num'>Compliance</th><th class='num'>Requirement</th><th class='num'>Burden</th><th class='num'>Six-term total</th><th class='num'>Per 100k</th><th class='num'>Change</th></tr>$($yearRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>Raw totals combine frequency and report volume; the per-100,000 column is the preferred comparison. Because the same companies appear in every year, this table supports a cleaner longitudinal reading than an unbalanced archive.</p></div>
<div class='panel'><h3>Quantified reading of the time series</h3><p>Across the balanced panel, the six-term rate changes from <strong>$(One $rate[2015])</strong> per 100,000 words in 2015 to <strong>$(One $rate[2025])</strong> in 2025, a net change of <strong>$('{0:+0.0;-0.0;0.0}%' -f $overallChange)</strong>. The early-period average (2015-2019) is <strong>$(One $earlyAvg)</strong>, compared with <strong>$(One $lateAvg)</strong> for 2021-2025. The index rose in <strong>$rising of 10</strong> year-to-year intervals; the largest absolute movement occurred in <strong>$($largestJump.Year)</strong> (<strong>$('{0:+0.0;-0.0;0.0}%' -f $largestJump.Change)</strong>, from $(One $largestJump.From) to $(One $largestJump.To)). These are changes in normalized disclosure frequency, not estimates of cost.</p><p>The detailed term table below helps distinguish broadening vocabulary from a single-word effect. It reports each term's total count, average annual rate, start/end rate and its high and low years. A term can rise while the combined index is flat if another term falls or if report length changes.</p></div>
 <div class='panel'><h3>Term-by-term trend statistics</h3><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Term family</th><th class='num'>2015-2025 count</th><th class='num'>Mean annual incidence</th><th class='num'>2015 incidence</th><th class='num'>2025 incidence</th><th class='num'>Net change</th><th>Peak year (incidence)</th><th>Lowest year (incidence)</th></tr>$($termRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>Incidence is calculated after aggregating all reports in a year and dividing by that year's total extracted words. This avoids giving a short report the same weight as a long report when computing annual incidence.</p></div>
 <div class='panel'><h3>Annual leaders across three lenses</h3><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Year</th><th>Highest-incidence term</th><th class='num'>Incidence/100k</th><th>Most coded theme</th><th class='num'>Theme passages</th><th>Most common frame</th><th class='num'>Frame share</th></tr>$($termTrendRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>This table places lexical incidence beside the thematic and rhetorical coding. When the same frame or theme persists while the leading term changes, that suggests continuity in how regulation is organised even as the vocabulary shifts.</p></div>
<h2>3. Thematic coding</h2><div class='panel'><h3>Theme prevalence across the balanced corpus</h3><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Theme</th><th class='num'>Coded passages</th><th class='num'>Companies mentioning</th><th>Share of theme assignments</th></tr>$($themeRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>Themes are overlapping: one passage may count under several themes. The percentages therefore describe the distribution of theme assignments, not mutually exclusive shares. "Compliance and governance" captures internal oversight; "reporting, disclosure and assurance" captures the documentation and verification infrastructure around obligations; "direct cost and resourcing" captures passages that explicitly connect rules to money, staff, fees, complexity or resource pressure.</p></div>
<div class='panel'><h3>Relative weight of the six tracked terms</h3><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Term family</th><th class='num'>Corpus count</th><th class='num'>Share of six-term total</th></tr>$($termShareRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>This distribution is a useful guard against over-reading the aggregate line. If procedural words dominate the corpus, the index is primarily a measure of compliance vocabulary and governance disclosure, rather than an index of explicit regulatory frustration.</p></div>
<div class='panel'><h3>How themes change by year</h3><p>The annual leaders table above reports the single most frequent theme. Because theme assignments overlap, a change in the leader does not mean other themes disappear. It identifies which organisational response is most visible in that year's coded passages and can highlight periods in which reporting, systems, climate, privacy or prudential language becomes more prominent.</p><p>In substantive terms, a recurring pairing of compliance/governance with systems/data indicates that regulation is being absorbed into operating infrastructure. A recurring cost/resourcing code alongside obligation/control indicates that companies acknowledge implementation work without necessarily presenting a separately quantified "regulatory cost" line.</p></div>
<h2>4. Frame analysis</h2><div class='two'><div class='panel'><h3>Primary frames</h3><table><tr><th>Frame</th><th class='num'>Passages</th><th class='num'>Share</th></tr>$($frameRows.ToString())</table></div><div class='panel'><h3>Interpretation</h3><p><strong>Cost or challenge</strong> treats regulation as expense, complexity, delay, risk or resource pressure.</p><p><strong>Obligation or control</strong> presents compliance as managed through policies, controls, monitoring, audits or mandated actions.</p><p><strong>Transition or anticipation</strong> looks forward to proposed, evolving or newly effective rules and preparation work.</p><p><strong>Opportunity or legitimacy</strong> links responsible compliance to trust, leadership, access or value creation.</p><p><strong>Descriptive or neutral</strong> records a regulatory fact without a clear evaluative or forward-looking signal.</p></div></div><div class='panel'><p>The most frequent frame is <strong>$(H $topFrame.Key)</strong>, accounting for <strong>$(Num $topFrame.Value)</strong> selected passages. This is consistent with a narrative in which companies operationalise regulation through governance routines and control systems rather than describing it as a standalone financial line item.</p></div>
 <h2>5. Company comparison</h2><div class='panel'><p>Companies are ranked by their aggregate six-term incidence per 100,000 extracted words across all 11 reports, highest first. This ordering makes the comparison about normalized regulatory-language incidence rather than total document volume. Sector and legally required disclosure remain important confounders, so the ranking is descriptive rather than a league table of actual compliance cost.</p><div class='company-filter-controls'><label for='company-sector-filter'>Filter by sector</label><select id='company-sector-filter'>$companySectorOptions</select><label for='company-subsector-filter'>Filter by subsector</label><select id='company-subsector-filter'>$companySubsectorOptions</select><span id='company-filter-summary' class='small' aria-live='polite'>Showing all companies</span></div><p class='interactive-hint'>Choose a broad sector, a specific ASX industry-group subsector, or both. The rank remains the company's overall balanced-panel rank; the subsector list uses the underlying industry-group labels from the local ASX listing snapshot.</p><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table id='company-comparison-table'><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Company</th><th class='num'>Reports</th><th class='num'>Words</th><th class='num'>Six-term incidence/100k</th><th class='num'>SD across years</th></tr>$($companyRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>The SD column is the standard deviation of each company's 11 annual six-term incidences. It describes year-to-year volatility in disclosure incidence, not volatility in actual compliance expenditure.</p></div>
<h2>7. Illustrative passages</h2><div class='panel'><p>These short extracts are selected for coding clarity from the balanced panel. They illustrate how reports talk about regulatory work; they do not estimate the size of a company's compliance cost.</p><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table class='evidence'><tr><th>Company and year</th><th>Themes</th><th>Frame</th><th>Illustrative extract</th><th>Source</th></tr>$($evidenceRows.ToString())</table></div></div>
<h2>8. What the balanced series suggests</h2><div class='panel'><p>Three broad patterns can be read from this consistent 2015-2025 group. First, regulatory language is usually procedural: reports emphasise controls, assurance, reporting, monitoring and systems that make obligations executable. Second, explicit cost language is narrower than the wider compliance infrastructure, so a low "burden" count should not be interpreted as low regulatory effort. Third, the year trend should be read as changing disclosure salience: a higher normalized rate suggests regulation occupies more textual space, potentially because rules are changing, reporting expectations are expanding, or companies are making systems and governance more visible.</p><p>The highest-frequency theme in this corpus is <strong>$(H $topTheme.Key)</strong> ($(Num $topTheme.Value) theme assignments). This supports a narrative of regulation as an embedded management practice: external rules are translated into internal accountabilities, data and controls, with costs often appearing indirectly through audit fees, technology, staffing, implementation and assurance.</p><h3>Additional patterns worth investigating</h3><ul><li><strong>Proceduralisation:</strong> the gap between the broad compliance infrastructure and the explicit burden vocabulary suggests that companies commonly narrate regulation as a control problem to be managed rather than a cost to be contested.</li><li><strong>Disclosure intensity versus report size:</strong> the normalized rate should be read alongside word totals. A year with more regulatory terms but fewer words indicates a change in salience, while simultaneous growth in both may reflect expanding report architecture.</li><li><strong>Concentration:</strong> the term-share table identifies whether the corpus is driven by "regulation" and "compliance" or by the more operational "requirement" and "legislation" families. That distinction helps separate direct legal vocabulary from implementation vocabulary.</li><li><strong>Heterogeneity:</strong> the cross-company spread table shows whether the panel trend is broad-based or dominated by a small number of highly regulated sectors. Follow-up work can stratify the panel by industry and compare within-sector changes.</li><li><strong>Event-sensitive peaks:</strong> unusually large year-to-year movements are candidates for close reading of contemporaneous regulatory reforms, climate and sustainability standards, privacy/cyber incidents, prudential changes or major transactions.</li></ul></div>
<h2>9. Interpretation guide and limitations</h2><div class='panel'><p>The report supports a careful narrative: regulatory burden is visible in annual reports primarily through the organisational machinery built to comply. Companies describe obligations, controls, assurance, systems, monitoring, data and reporting more often than they attach a single dollar amount to "regulatory compliance." The per-100,000 index makes the changing prominence of that vocabulary visible, while the term-specific, thematic and frame tables show what kind of language is moving.</p><p>The balanced-panel restriction improves comparability but reduces coverage by excluding incomplete companies. Keyword and rule-based coding can overcount boilerplate and cannot distinguish legal necessity from voluntary best practice. PDF extraction can lose image-only text or scramble complex tables. The results are therefore disclosure-text measures and should be paired with close reading, industry controls and financial data before making claims about actual regulatory expenditure, regulatory effectiveness or causal effects of a particular law.</p></div>
<footer>Generated from the local PDFs in <code>$archiveDisplay</code>. Report eligibility and counts are reproducible from the script <code>generate-balanced-regulatory-report.ps1</code>; links open the corresponding local annual report.</footer></main></body></html>
"@
$sectorHtml=@"
<h2>7. Regulatory language by sector</h2><div class='panel'><p>Companies are grouped into broad GICS-style sectors using the local ASX listing snapshot, with transparent fallbacks for historical or renamed tickers. The same sector rules are used in both the ASX50 and ASX200 reports. However, each report has its own complete-company eligibility screen, so the companies represented inside a sector can differ between panels; a one-company sector row means one eligible company in that panel, not a different sector definition. The chart and table show how the six-term index changes within each sector. A sector rate reflects both the language used and the reporting conventions, legal obligations and business activities concentrated in that sector; it is not a measure of sector-wide compliance expenditure.</p><h3>Six-term rate by sector, 2015-2025</h3><div class='chart'><svg viewBox='0 0 1000 340' role='img' aria-label='Six tracked regulatory terms per 100,000 words by sector from 2015 through 2025'>$( $sectorGrid.ToString() )$( $sectorSeries.ToString() )$( $labels.ToString() )<text x='515' y='326' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' fill='#5b6770'>Six tracked terms per 100,000 extracted words; y-axis $(One $sectorYMin)-$(One $sectorYMax)</text></svg></div><div class='legend sector-legend'>$($sectorLegend.ToString())</div><button type='button' class='sector-reset' id='sector-reset'>Show all sectors</button><p class='interactive-hint'>Select a sector label to isolate that line and reduce visual overlap; select it again or use &quot;Show all sectors&quot; to restore the full comparison.</p><p class='caption'>Each line aggregates all complete companies assigned to that sector in each year. The relative slope is the clearest comparison: it shows whether regulatory vocabulary became more or less prominent within a sector over the period. Lines can cross because report length, sector mix and disclosure requirements differ.</p><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Sector</th><th class='num'>Companies</th><th class='num'>Reports</th><th class='num'>Words</th><th class='num'>Mean rate/100k</th><th class='num'>2015 rate</th><th class='num'>2025 rate</th><th class='num'>Change</th></tr>$($sectorRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>The mean rate is calculated from pooled sector words across all 11 years. The 2015 and 2025 columns provide the endpoints for the chart; the change column is the endpoint percentage change.</p></div>
<h2>8. Headquarters geography</h2><div class='panel'><p>This second categorisation groups companies by the broad region of their principal corporate headquarters or primary corporate office. It is deliberately different from sector: it helps distinguish language associated with Australian state-based regulatory settings and reporting cultures from language associated with New Zealand or overseas-headquartered parent companies. Headquarters location does not describe where a company operates; many firms have substantial operations across multiple jurisdictions.</p><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>HQ region</th><th class='num'>Companies</th><th class='num'>Mean rate/100k</th><th class='num'>2015 rate</th><th class='num'>2025 rate</th><th class='num'>Change</th><th>Largest sector group</th><th>Companies in group</th></tr>$($hqRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>Australian state labels are broad headquarters regions; overseas groups are reported at country-level where a parent company's principal office is outside Australia. Rates are descriptive text-salience comparisons and should not be interpreted as evidence that one jurisdiction imposes a particular cost level.</p></div>
"@
$sectorMarker="<h2>8. Headquarters geography</h2>"
if($sectorHtml.Contains($sectorMarker)){$sectorHtml=$sectorHtml.Substring(0,$sectorHtml.IndexOf($sectorMarker))}
$exposureHtml=@"
<h2>8. Domestic versus multinational exposure</h2><div class='panel'><p>Companies are grouped according to whether their annual reports describe a primarily Australia/New Zealand operating footprint or material operations, revenue, assets or customers across multiple international markets. This is a business-footprint grouping, not a headquarters measure. It helps test whether multinational complexity is associated with a higher or changing regulatory-language rate, while recognising that international companies also differ in sector, size and reporting obligations.</p><h3>Six-term rate by operating footprint</h3><div class='chart'><svg viewBox='0 0 1000 340' role='img' aria-label='Six tracked regulatory terms per 100,000 words for home-market focused and multinational companies from 2015 through 2025'>$( $exposureGrid.ToString() )$( $exposureSeries.ToString() )$( $labels.ToString() )<text x='515' y='326' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' fill='#5b6770'>Six tracked terms per 100,000 extracted words; y-axis $(One $exposureYMin)-$(One $exposureYMax)</text></svg></div><div class='legend'>$($exposureLegend.ToString())</div><p class='caption'>Each line aggregates companies assigned to the same operating-footprint category in every year. The endpoint and slope comparisons show whether regulatory vocabulary is more prominent or changes differently for multinational businesses than for companies focused primarily on their home market.</p><div style='overflow-x:auto'><table><tr><th>Exposure group</th><th class='num'>Companies</th><th class='num'>Reports</th><th class='num'>Words</th><th class='num'>Mean rate/100k</th><th class='num'>2015 rate</th><th class='num'>2025 rate</th><th class='num'>Change</th><th>Most coded theme</th><th>Most common frame</th></tr>$($exposureRows.ToString())</table></div><p class='caption'>The classification is a transparent research grouping based on the reported geographic footprint; it is not a financial or legal determination. Borderline trans-Tasman businesses are treated as home-market focused, while material operations beyond Australia/New Zealand are treated as multinational.</p></div>
"@
$interactiveHtml=@"
<h2>9. Distribution of regulatory-term incidence</h2><div class='panel'><p>This histogram shows how company-level six-term incidence is distributed in the selected year. Each bar counts companies whose annual report rate falls within that interval; it complements the pooled annual line by showing whether a year-wide movement is broad-based or concentrated in a smaller tail of companies.</p><div class='chart'><svg id='rate-histogram' viewBox='0 0 920 320' role='img' aria-label='Histogram of company-level six-term regulatory salience per 100,000 words'></svg></div><div class='hist-controls'><label for='histogram-year'>Select year</label><select id='histogram-year'>$histOptions</select><button type='button' class='hist-outlier-toggle' id='hist-toggle-outliers'>Remove &gt;3 sigma outliers</button></div><div id='hist-summary' class='hist-summary' aria-live='polite'></div><div id='hist-outliers' class='hist-outliers' aria-live='polite'></div><p class='caption'>The selector redraws the distribution for each year from the same balanced panel. The orange curve is a fitted normal distribution using that year's mean (&mu;) and standard deviation (&sigma;); dashed purple markers show &plusmn;1&sigma; either side of the mean. The outlier button excludes companies whose rate is more than 3&sigma; from the mean and lists them below the chart.</p></div>
"@
$ocrNote="<div class='callout'><strong>Targeted OCR corrections.</strong> A small number of reports with severe font-encoding loss were rescanned with OCR for the six tracked term families. Their verified word denominators are retained unless the original text layer was demonstrably incomplete; the original PDFs remain unchanged. These targeted corrections improve term recognition but do not imply that every OCR character is perfect.</div>"
$html=$html.Replace("<h2>1. Scope and coding method</h2>",$ocrNote+"<h2>1. Scope and coding method</h2>").Replace("<h2>7. Illustrative passages</h2>",$sectorHtml+$exposureHtml+$interactiveHtml+"<h2>11. Illustrative passages</h2>").Replace("<h2>8. What the balanced series suggests</h2>","<h2>12. What the balanced series suggests</h2>").Replace("<h2>9. Interpretation guide and limitations</h2>","<h2>13. Interpretation guide and limitations</h2>")
$interactiveScript=@"
<script>
(function(){
  var moversData=$moversJson;
  var moverPanel=document.getElementById('mover-panel');
  function esc(value){return String(value).replace(/&/g,'&amp;').replace(/</g,'&lt;').replace(/>/g,'&gt;').replace(/\"/g,'&quot;');}
  function renderMovers(year){
    if(!moverPanel){return;}
    var rows=moversData[String(year)]||[];
    if(!rows.length){moverPanel.innerHTML='<h4>'+esc(year)+'</h4><p class="small">No prior-year comparison is available for this point.</p>';return;}
    var html='<h4>'+esc(year)+' - five biggest company-level movers from the previous year</h4><ol class="mover-list">';
    rows.forEach(function(row){var ch=Number(row.Change);var sign=ch>=0?'+':'';html+='<li><strong>'+esc(row.Ticker)+' - '+esc(row.Name)+'</strong>: '+Number(row.Rate).toFixed(1)+' terms/100,000; <span class="change">'+sign+ch.toFixed(1)+'%</span> from '+Number(row.Previous).toFixed(1)+'</li>';});
    moverPanel.innerHTML=html+'</ol>';
  }
  document.querySelectorAll('.main-rate-point').forEach(function(point){point.addEventListener('mouseenter',function(){renderMovers(point.dataset.year);});point.addEventListener('focus',function(){renderMovers(point.dataset.year);});});
  renderMovers(2025);

  var panelScopeToggle=document.getElementById('panel-scope-toggle'),panelScopeLabel=document.getElementById('panel-scope-label'),asx50Only=false;
  var companySectorFilter=document.getElementById('company-sector-filter'),companySubsectorFilter=document.getElementById('company-subsector-filter'),companyFilterSummary=document.getElementById('company-filter-summary');
  var companyRows=Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#company-comparison-table tr[data-company-sector]'));
  function syncCompanySubsectors(){
    if(!companySubsectorFilter){return;}
    var selected=companySectorFilter?companySectorFilter.value:'',current=companySubsectorFilter.value,seen={};
    companyRows.forEach(function(row){if((!selected||row.dataset.companySector===selected)&&row.dataset.companySubsector){seen[row.dataset.companySubsector]=true;}});
    var values=Object.keys(seen).sort();companySubsectorFilter.innerHTML='<option value="">All subsectors</option>'+values.map(function(v){return '<option value="'+esc(v)+'">'+esc(v)+'</option>';}).join('');
    companySubsectorFilter.value=seen[current]?current:'';
  }
  function applyCompanySectorFilter(){
    if(!companySectorFilter&&!companySubsectorFilter){return;}
    var selected=companySectorFilter?companySectorFilter.value:'',selectedSubsector=companySubsectorFilter?companySubsectorFilter.value:'',visible=0;
    companyRows.forEach(function(row){var inScope=!asx50Only||row.dataset.asx50==='true';var show=inScope&&(!selected||row.dataset.companySector===selected)&&(!selectedSubsector||row.dataset.companySubsector===selectedSubsector);row.style.display=show?'':'none';if(show){visible++;}});
    if(companyFilterSummary){var labels=[];if(asx50Only){labels.push('ASX50');}if(selected){labels.push(selected);}if(selectedSubsector){labels.push(selectedSubsector);}companyFilterSummary.textContent=labels.length?(visible+' compan'+(visible===1?'y':'ies')+' shown in '+labels.join(' / ')):('Showing all '+visible+' companies');}
  }
  if(companySectorFilter){companySectorFilter.addEventListener('change',function(){syncCompanySubsectors();applyCompanySectorFilter();});}if(companySubsectorFilter){companySubsectorFilter.addEventListener('change',applyCompanySectorFilter);}syncCompanySubsectors();applyCompanySectorFilter();
  if(panelScopeToggle){panelScopeToggle.addEventListener('click',function(){asx50Only=!asx50Only;panelScopeToggle.textContent=asx50Only?'Show ASX200':'Show ASX50 only';if(panelScopeLabel){panelScopeLabel.textContent=asx50Only?'ASX50':'ASX200';}var q200=document.getElementById('quantified-reading-asx200'),q50=document.getElementById('quantified-reading-asx50');if(q200){q200.style.display=asx50Only?'none':'';}if(q50){q50.style.display=asx50Only?'':'none';}renderScopeMetrics();applyCompanySectorFilter();renderAnnualScope();renderSectorScope();});}

  var sectorLines=Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.sector-line'));
  var sectorButtons=Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.sector-toggle'));
  var selectedSector=null;
  function applySector(){sectorLines.forEach(function(line){var active=!selectedSector||line.dataset.sector===selectedSector;line.classList.toggle('is-muted',!active);line.classList.toggle('is-active',!!selectedSector&&active);});sectorButtons.forEach(function(button){var active=!selectedSector||button.dataset.sector===selectedSector;button.classList.toggle('is-muted',!active);button.classList.toggle('is-active',!!selectedSector&&active);});}
  sectorButtons.forEach(function(button){button.addEventListener('click',function(){selectedSector=selectedSector===button.dataset.sector?null:button.dataset.sector;applySector();});});
  var sectorReset=document.getElementById('sector-reset');if(sectorReset){sectorReset.addEventListener('click',function(){selectedSector=null;applySector();});}applySector();

  var scopeData=$scopeJson;
  function numberText(value){return Number(value).toLocaleString(undefined,{maximumFractionDigits:1});}
  function renderScopeMetrics(){var rows=[],ticks={};Object.keys(scopeData).forEach(function(y){(scopeData[y]||[]).forEach(function(row){if(!asx50Only||row.IsASX50===true){rows.push(row);ticks[row.Ticker]=true;}});});var words=rows.reduce(function(a,row){return a+Number(row.Words||0);},0);var reportsEl=document.getElementById('scope-metric-reports'),companiesEl=document.getElementById('scope-metric-companies'),wordsEl=document.getElementById('scope-metric-words');if(reportsEl)reportsEl.textContent=numberText(rows.length);if(companiesEl)companiesEl.textContent=numberText(Object.keys(ticks).length);if(wordsEl)wordsEl.textContent=numberText(words);}
  var annualSvg=document.getElementById('annual-incidence-chart'),annualLine=document.getElementById('annual-incidence-line'),annualPoints=annualSvg?Array.prototype.slice.call(annualSvg.querySelectorAll('.main-rate-point')):[],annualYMin=$yMin,annualYMax=$yMax;
  function scopedRate(rows){var words=0,terms=0;rows.forEach(function(row){var w=Number(row.Words);if(w>0&&isFinite(w)){words+=w;terms+=Number(row.Rate)*w/100000;}});return words?100000*terms/words:0;}
  function renderAnnualScope(){if(!annualLine||!annualPoints.length)return;var vals=annualPoints.map(function(point){var y=point.dataset.year;return scopedRate((scopeData[String(y)]||[]).filter(function(row){return !asx50Only||row.IsASX50===true;}));});var points=vals.map(function(v,i){var x=100+(930-100)*i/(vals.length-1),yy=275-((v-annualYMin)/(annualYMax-annualYMin))*240;return x.toFixed(1)+','+yy.toFixed(1);});annualLine.setAttribute('points',points.join(' '));annualPoints.forEach(function(point,i){var y=annualYMin;var yy=275-((vals[i]-annualYMin)/(annualYMax-annualYMin))*240;point.setAttribute('cy',yy.toFixed(1));var title=point.querySelector('title');if(title){title.textContent=point.dataset.year+': '+vals[i].toFixed(1)+' terms per 100,000 words. Hover for top five company movers.';}});}
  function renderSectorScope(){if(!sectorLines||!sectorLines.length)return;var sectorYMin=$sectorYMin,sectorYMax=$sectorYMax,yearsForSector=annualPoints.map(function(point){return point.dataset.year;});sectorLines.forEach(function(line){var sec=line.dataset.sector,points=yearsForSector.map(function(y,i){var rows=(scopeData[String(y)]||[]).filter(function(row){return row.Sector===sec&&(!asx50Only||row.IsASX50===true);});var v=scopedRate(rows),x=100+(930-100)*i/(yearsForSector.length-1),yy=275-((v-sectorYMin)/(sectorYMax-sectorYMin))*240;return x.toFixed(1)+','+yy.toFixed(1);});line.setAttribute('points',points.join(' '));});}
  var histSvg=document.getElementById('rate-histogram');var histSummary=document.getElementById('hist-summary');var histSelect=document.getElementById('histogram-year');var histOutliers=document.getElementById('hist-outliers');var histToggle=document.getElementById('hist-toggle-outliers');var removeOutliers=false;var currentHistogramYear=histSelect?histSelect.value:'2015';
  function svgEl(tag,attrs,text){var el=document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg',tag);Object.keys(attrs||{}).forEach(function(key){el.setAttribute(key,attrs[key]);});if(text!==undefined){el.textContent=text;}return el;}
  function stats(values){var mean=values.reduce(function(a,b){return a+b;},0)/values.length;var variance=values.reduce(function(a,b){return a+(b-mean)*(b-mean);},0)/values.length;var sorted=values.slice().sort(function(a,b){return a-b;});return {mean:mean,sd:Math.sqrt(variance),median:sorted[Math.floor((sorted.length-1)/2)],min:sorted[0],max:sorted[sorted.length-1]};}
  function renderHistogram(year){
    currentHistogramYear=String(year);if(!histSvg){return;}while(histSvg.firstChild){histSvg.removeChild(histSvg.firstChild);}
    var rows=(scopeData[String(year)]||[]).filter(function(row){return !asx50Only||row.IsASX50===true;});var observations=rows.map(function(row){return {row:row,rate:Number(row.Rate)};}).filter(function(item){return isFinite(item.rate);});
    if(!observations.length){if(histSummary){histSummary.textContent='No company observations are available for '+year+'.';}if(histOutliers){histOutliers.innerHTML='';}return;}
    var allRates=observations.map(function(item){return item.rate;}),allStats=stats(allRates),threshold=3*allStats.sd;var outliers=observations.filter(function(item){return allStats.sd>0&&Math.abs(item.rate-allStats.mean)>threshold;});var used=removeOutliers?observations.filter(function(item){return !(allStats.sd>0&&Math.abs(item.rate-allStats.mean)>threshold);}):observations;var rates=used.map(function(item){return item.rate;});if(!rates.length){rates=allRates;}
    var st=stats(rates);var min=st.min,max=st.max;if(max===min){max=min+1;}var bins=16,step=(max-min)/bins,counts=[];for(var i=0;i<bins;i++){counts.push(0);}rates.forEach(function(value){var index=Math.min(bins-1,Math.max(0,Math.floor((value-min)/step)));counts[index]++;});
    var W=920,H=320,left=70,right=20,top=22,bottom=62,plotW=W-left-right,plotH=H-top-bottom,maxCount=Math.max.apply(null,counts);histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('line',{x1:left,x2:left+plotW,y1:top+plotH,y2:top+plotH,stroke:'#82919b'}));histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('line',{x1:left,x2:left,y1:top,y2:top+plotH,stroke:'#82919b'}));
    for(var gy=0;gy<=4;gy++){var gv=maxCount*gy/4,gyy=top+plotH-plotH*gy/4;histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('line',{x1:left,x2:left+plotW,y1:gyy,y2:gyy,stroke:'#dce3e8'}));histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('text',{x:left-9,y:gyy+4,'text-anchor':'end',class:'axis-label'},String(Math.round(gv))));}
    counts.forEach(function(count,index){var x=left+index*plotW/bins+2,w=plotW/bins-4,h=maxCount?count/maxCount*plotH:0,y=top+plotH-h;var rect=svgEl('rect',{x:x,y:y,width:w,height:h,class:'hist-bar'});rect.appendChild(svgEl('title',{},count+' companies: '+numberText(min+index*step)+' to '+numberText(min+(index+1)*step)+' terms per 100,000'));histSvg.appendChild(rect);if(index%2===0||index===bins-1){histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('text',{x:x+w/2,y:top+plotH+18,'text-anchor':'middle',class:'axis-label'},numberText(min+index*step)));}});
    var xFor=function(value){return left+Math.max(0,Math.min(1,(value-min)/(max-min)))*plotW;};var yForCount=function(value){return top+plotH-(maxCount?value/maxCount*plotH:0);};var meanX=xFor(st.mean);histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('line',{x1:meanX,x2:meanX,y1:top,y2:top+plotH,class:'hist-mean-line'}));histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('text',{x:meanX+4,y:top+14,class:'hist-mean-label'},'Mean'));[-3,-2,-1,1,2,3].forEach(function(multiplier){var sigmaValue=st.mean+multiplier*st.sd;if(sigmaValue>=min&&sigmaValue<=max){var sx=xFor(sigmaValue);histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('line',{x1:sx,x2:sx,y1:top,y2:top+plotH,class:'hist-sigma-line','data-sigma':multiplier}));}});
    if(st.sd>0){var path='';for(var pi=0;pi<=100;pi++){var xv=min+(max-min)*pi/100;var z=(xv-st.mean)/st.sd;var density=Math.exp(-0.5*z*z)/(st.sd*Math.sqrt(2*Math.PI));var expected=density*rates.length*step;var px=xFor(xv),py=yForCount(expected);path+=(pi===0?'M':'L')+px.toFixed(2)+' '+py.toFixed(2)+' ';}histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('path',{d:path,class:'hist-curve'}));}
    histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('text',{x:left+plotW/2,y:H-8,'text-anchor':'middle',class:'axis-label'},'Company six-term salience per 100,000 words'));histSvg.appendChild(svgEl('text',{x:16,y:top+plotH/2,transform:'rotate(-90 16 '+(top+plotH/2)+')','text-anchor':'middle',class:'axis-label'},'Companies'));
    if(histSummary){histSummary.textContent=year+': '+rates.length+' companies shown; mean '+numberText(st.mean)+', median '+numberText(st.median)+', sigma '+numberText(st.sd)+', range '+numberText(st.min)+' - '+numberText(st.max)+' terms per 100,000 words.'+(removeOutliers?' '+outliers.length+' >3-sigma outliers removed.':' '+outliers.length+' >3-sigma outliers detected.');}
    if(histOutliers){var outHtml='<h4>'+outliers.length+' companies beyond 3 standard deviations</h4>';if(outliers.length){outHtml+='<ul>'+outliers.sort(function(a,b){return Math.abs(b.rate-allStats.mean)-Math.abs(a.rate-allStats.mean);}).map(function(item){return '<li><strong>'+esc(item.row.Ticker)+' - '+esc(item.row.Name)+'</strong>: '+numberText(item.rate)+' terms/100,000 (mean '+numberText(allStats.mean)+', '+(item.rate>=allStats.mean?'+':'')+numberText((item.rate-allStats.mean)/allStats.sd)+' sigma)</li>';}).join('')+'</ul>';}else{outHtml+='<p class="small">No company falls beyond the 3-sigma threshold in this year.</p>';}histOutliers.innerHTML=outHtml;}
  }
  if(histToggle){histToggle.addEventListener('click',function(){removeOutliers=!removeOutliers;histToggle.textContent=removeOutliers?'Restore outliers':'Remove >3 sigma outliers';renderHistogram(currentHistogramYear);});}
  if(histSelect){histSelect.addEventListener('change',function(){currentHistogramYear=histSelect.value;renderHistogram(currentHistogramYear);});renderHistogram(currentHistogramYear||'2015');var hp=histSelect.parentNode.parentNode.querySelector('.caption');if(hp)hp.innerHTML='The fitted orange curve uses the selected year\'s mean and standard deviation. The pink vertical line is the <strong>Mean</strong>; gray dashed guides mark ±1σ, ±2σ and ±3σ where visible. The button excludes companies more than 3σ from the mean and lists them below.';}
})();
</script>
"@
$html=$html.Replace('</body>',$interactiveScript+'</body>')
# Keep the delivered report focused on the requested analytical sequence.  The
# The delivered report is limited to the three retained incidence sections.
function Get-RenderedSection([string]$source,[string]$pattern){
  $m=[regex]::Match($source,"(?s)<h2>$pattern.*?(?=<h2>|<footer>)")
  if($m.Success){return $m.Value}else{return ''}
}
$prefix=$html.Substring(0,$html.IndexOf('<h2>1. Scope and coding method</h2>'))
$prefix=$prefix.Replace($ocrNote,'')
$yearSection=Get-RenderedSection $html '2\. Corpus and year-by-year content analysis'
$quantifiedMatch=[regex]::Match($yearSection,"(?s)<div class='panel'><h3>Quantified reading of the time series</h3>.*?</div>")
if($quantifiedMatch.Success){$yearSection=$yearSection.Replace($quantifiedMatch.Value,'');$graphMarker="<div class='panel'><h3>Which regulatory words drive the index?</h3>";$graphInsert=$yearSection.IndexOf($graphMarker);if($graphInsert -ge 0){$yearSection=$yearSection.Insert($graphInsert,$quantifiedMatch.Value)}}
$sectorSection=Get-RenderedSection $html '7\. Regulatory language by sector'
$companySection=Get-RenderedSection $html '5\. Company comparison'
$yearSection=$yearSection.Replace('<h2>2. Corpus and year-by-year content analysis</h2>','<h2>1. Year-by-year analysis</h2>')
$sectorSection=$sectorSection.Replace('<h2>7. Regulatory language by sector</h2>','<h2>2. Analysis by sector</h2>')
$companySection=$companySection.Replace('<h2>5. Company comparison</h2>','<h2>3. Company comparison</h2>')
$leaderIndex=$yearSection.IndexOf("<div class='panel'><h3>Annual leaders across three lenses</h3>")
if($leaderIndex -ge 0){$yearSection=$yearSection.Substring(0,$leaderIndex)}
$yearSection=[regex]::Replace($yearSection,"<div class='metric'><div class='n'>[^<]*</div><div class='l'>coded regulatory passages</div></div>",'')
$scriptBlock=[regex]::Match($html,'(?s)<script>.*?</script>\s*</body>').Value
$footer="<footer>Generated from the local PDFs in <code>$archiveDisplay</code>. The report is limited to the three retained incidence sections.</footer>"
$html=$prefix+$yearSection+$sectorSection+$companySection+$footer+'</main>'+$scriptBlock+'</html>'
$html=$html.Replace('</style></head>', '.panel-toggle{display:inline-block;padding:6px 11px;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:#1769aa;color:#fff;cursor:pointer;font:inherit}.panel-toggle:hover{background:#12334d}</style></head>')
# Add stable hooks to the summary metrics so the ASX200 in-page scope toggle can
# recalculate the information row without loading the separate ASX50 report.
$html=$html.Replace("<div class='metric'><div class='n'>$($total.Reports)</div>","<div class='metric'><div id='scope-metric-reports' class='n'>$($total.Reports)</div>")
$html=$html.Replace("<div class='metric'><div class='n'>$($complete.Count)</div>","<div class='metric'><div id='scope-metric-companies' class='n'>$($complete.Count)</div>")
$html=$html.Replace("<div class='metric'><div class='n'>$(Num $total.Words)</div>","<div class='metric'><div id='scope-metric-words' class='n'>$(Num $total.Words)</div>")
$html=$html.Replace("<div class='metric'><div class='n'>$(Num $total.Coded)</div>","<div class='metric'><div id='scope-metric-coded' class='n'>$(Num $total.Coded)</div>")
$html=$html.Replace('<p>Across the balanced panel, the six-term rate changes','<p id="quantified-reading-asx200">Across the balanced panel, the six-term rate changes')
$quantifiedAsx50Html='</p><p id="quantified-reading-asx50" style="display:none">'+$asx50Narrative+'</p><p>The detailed term table below helps distinguish broadening vocabulary from a single-word effect.'
$html=$html.Replace('</p><p>The detailed term table below helps distinguish broadening vocabulary from a single-word effect.',$quantifiedAsx50Html)
# Use one reader-facing term throughout the delivered report.  Internal variable
# names and JSON field names remain unchanged for compatibility with the extractor.
$incidenceReplacements=@(
  @('Six-term regulatory salience','Six-term regulatory incidence'), @('six-term regulatory salience','six-term regulatory incidence'),
  @('six-term salience','six-term incidence'), @('regulatory-language salience','regulatory-language incidence'),
  @('disclosure salience','disclosure incidence'), @('textual salience','textual incidence'),
  @('annual rate','annual incidence'), @('Mean annual rate','Mean annual incidence'),
  @('Highest-rate term','Highest-incidence term'), @('Highest-rate','Highest-incidence'),
  @('rate/100k','incidence/100k'), @('Rate/100k','Incidence/100k'),
  @(' rate per 100,000',' incidence per 100,000'), @(' rates per 100,000',' incidences per 100,000'),
  @(' rate points',' incidence points'), @('mean rate','mean incidence'), @('Mean rate','Mean incidence'),
  @('2015 rate','2015 incidence'), @('2025 rate','2025 incidence'),
  @('Peak year (rate)','Peak year (incidence)'), @('Lowest year (rate)','Lowest year (incidence)'),
  @('annual report rate','annual report incidence'), @('whose rate falls','whose incidence falls'),
  @('whose rate is','whose incidence is'), @('start/end rate','start/end incidence'),
  @('sector rate','sector incidence'), @('Six-term rate','Six-term incidence'), @('six-term rate','six-term incidence'),
  @('term rate','term incidence'), @('term rates','term incidences'), @('rate reflects','incidence reflects'),
  @('rate is more','incidence is more'), @('rate is calculated','incidence is calculated'),
  @('average rate','average incidence'), @('average six-term rate','average six-term incidence'),
  @('vertical rate scale','vertical incidence scale'), @('rate scale','incidence scale'), @('rate baseline','incidence baseline'),
  @('regulatory-term rate','regulatory-term incidence'), @('rate is a','incidence is a'), @('rate changes','incidence changes'),
  @('The rate peaks','The incidence peaks')
)
foreach($pair in $incidenceReplacements){$html=$html.Replace($pair[0],$pair[1])}
$html=$html.Replace('Most salient theme','Most coded theme').Replace('most salient theme','most coded theme')
$html=$html.Replace('Thematic coding, frame analysis and keyword content analysis','Keyword content analysis')
$html=$html.Replace('The selected companies discuss regulation mainly as an obligation translated into controls, reporting, systems and assurance; explicit references to "burden" are much rarer than references to requirements, regulators and compliance infrastructure.','Explicit references to "burden" are much rarer than references to requirements, regulators and compliance, so the incidence series should be read as disclosure vocabulary rather than observed regulatory expenditure.')
$html=$html.Replace('if(histSelect){renderHistogram(histSelect.value);}','')
$html=[regex]::Replace($html,'(?s)\s*var histSvg=document\.getElementById\(''rate-histogram''\).*?if\(histSelect\)\{.*?\}\r?\n','')
# Remove any legacy UTF-8/Latin-1 artefacts from the interactive caption and
# keep the standard-deviation description readable in every browser encoding.
$html=[regex]::Replace($html,'gray dashed guides mark [^\.]+ where visible\.','gray dashed guides show the one-, two- and three-standard-deviation guides where visible.')
$html=[regex]::Replace($html,'companies more than [^ ]+ from the mean','companies more than three standard deviations from the mean')
[IO.File]::WriteAllText($outPath,$html,(New-Object Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))
Write-Output "written=$outPath companies=$($complete.Count) reports=$($total.Reports) words=$($total.Words) coded=$($total.Coded)"
